docsData.en.sections = {"getting-started": {"pages": [{"id": "guide.start", "content": "<h1 id=\"getting-started\">Getting Started</h1>\n<p>This page covers the build matrix, how to run the tests, a minimal first frame, and how to tell whether the real Metal backend is active.</p>\n<h2 id=\"prerequisites\">Prerequisites</h2>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Requirement</th><th>Needed for</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td>CMake 3.20+</td><td>every build</td></tr>\n<tr><td>C++17 compiler</td><td>every build</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Python 3</td><td>regenerating <code>gl46.h</code>, <code>gl46_types.h</code>, <code>gl_dispatch_gen.cpp</code>, <code>gl_c_exports.cpp</code>, <code>gl_stubs_gen.cpp</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Xcode command line tools</td><td>macOS and iOS builds, Metal framework</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>glslangValidator</code> + <code>spirv-cross</code></td><td>optional; enables <code>test_spirv_chain_apple</code> and <code>test_converter_proof</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>xcrun metal</code></td><td>optional; enables offline MSL compilation checks in <code>test_converter_aquarium</code></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>The Null backend builds on any host, including Linux, because it compiles no Apple source at all.</p>\n<h2 id=\"build-matrix\">Build matrix</h2>\n<p>All four configurations are supported. <code>TGLMT_APPLE_METAL</code> defaults to <code>OFF</code>; turning it on is what pulls in <code>src/metal/AppleMetalBridge.mm</code> and links <code>-framework Metal</code>.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Configuration</th><th>Configure</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td>Host, Null backend (default)</td><td><code>cmake -S . -B build</code></td><td><code>libtglmt.a</code>, <code>libtglmt.dylib</code>, all tests</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Host, Apple Metal</td><td><code>cmake -S . -B build-apple -DTGLMT_APPLE_METAL=ON</code></td><td>same, plus real-GPU tests become active</td></tr>\n<tr><td>iOS device, arm64</td><td>see below</td><td><code>build-iphoneos/libtglmt.a</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>iOS device, shared dylib</td><td>see below</td><td><code>build-ios/libtglmt.dylib</code> arm64</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h3 id=\"host-null-backend\">Host, Null backend</h3>\n<pre><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button><code>cmake -S . -B build\ncmake --build build -j8</code></pre>\n<h3 id=\"host-apple-metal-macos\">Host, Apple Metal (macOS)</h3>\n<pre><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button><code>cmake -S . -B build-apple -DTGLMT_APPLE_METAL=ON\ncmake --build build-apple -j8</code></pre>\n<p>This configures CMake to enable Objective-C++, compile <code>AppleMetalBridge.mm</code> with ARC, define <code>TGLMT_APPLE_METAL=1</code>, and link <code>Metal</code>, <code>Foundation</code> and <code>QuartzCore</code>.</p>\n<h3 id=\"ios-device-arm64\">iOS device, arm64</h3>\n<p>Two equivalent invocations. The toolchain-file form is the one used by the root <code>Makefile</code> and is the recommended one, because it also forces <code>-miphoneos-version-min</code>:</p>\n<pre><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button><code>cmake -S . -B build-iphoneos \\\n  -DTGLMT_APPLE_METAL=ON \\\n  -DCMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE=apps/aquarium/ios_toolchain.cmake \\\n  -DIOS_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET=16.0 \\\n  -DTGLMT_BUILD_TESTS=OFF\ncmake --build build-iphoneos -j8</code></pre>\n<p>Direct form, without the toolchain file:</p>\n<pre><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button><code>cmake -S . -B build-ios \\\n  -DCMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME=iOS \\\n  -DCMAKE_OSX_SYSROOT=\"$(xcrun --sdk iphoneos --show-sdk-path)\" \\\n  -DCMAKE_OSX_ARCHITECTURES=arm64 \\\n  -DCMAKE_OSX_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET=16.0 \\\n  -DTGLMT_APPLE_METAL=ON \\\n  -DTGLMT_BUILD_TESTS=OFF\ncmake --build build-ios -j8</code></pre>\n<p>Architecture is <code>arm64</code> only. The deployment target defaults to <code>16.0</code> (<code>DEPLOY_TARGET</code> in the root <code>Makefile</code>, <code>IOS_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET</code> in <code>apps/aquarium/ios_toolchain.cmake</code>).</p>\n<p>For building the Aquarium benchmark app on iOS, including signing, see <a href=\"../../apps/aquarium/DEPLOY_IOS.md\"><code>apps/aquarium/DEPLOY_IOS.md</code></a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"library-outputs\">Library outputs</h2>\n<p>Both targets are built from the same source list.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Target</th><th>Type</th><th>Output</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td><code>tglmt</code></td><td>static</td><td><code>libtglmt.a</code></td><td>for apps that link directly</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>tglmt_shared</code></td><td>shared</td><td><code>libtglmt.dylib</code> → <code>libtglmt.0.dylib</code> → <code>libtglmt.0.1.0.dylib</code></td><td>for <code>dlopen</code>/<code>dlsym</code></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Symbol visibility is deliberately left at the C++ default (<code>CXX_VISIBILITY_PRESET default</code>, <code>VISIBILITY_INLINES_HIDDEN OFF</code>), because loaders resolve <code>gl*</code> names through <code>dlsym</code>. There are no <code>install()</code> rules; consume the artefacts straight out of the build directory.</p>\n<h2 id=\"tests\">Tests</h2>\n<p>Every file under <code>tests/unit/</code> and <code>tests/integration/</code> becomes both an executable and a CTest test named after the file stem.</p>\n<pre><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button><code>cmake --build build -j8\nctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure</code></pre>\n<p><code>make test</code> wraps this through <code>scripts/build_and_test.sh</code>, which additionally regenerates the GL headers from <code>docs/khronos/gl.xml</code> first (pass <code>--no-gen</code> to skip).</p>\n<p>Tests that need a GPU print <code>SKIP</code> and exit 0 when no GPU is present, so a Null-backend build and an Apple-backend build both report success on an unattended host.</p>\n<p>Relevant behaviours to know before reading the output:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Tests whose real assertions need a GPU are skipped, not failed, when the device is a</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Null device.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Tests that read the Minecraft shader corpus check that <code>TGLMT_CORPUS_DIR</code> exists and</li>\n</ul>\n<p>skip otherwise. The corpus is not committed; fetch it with <code>tests/corpus/fetch-corpus.sh</code>.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Tests that shell out to <code>glslangValidator</code>, <code>spirv-cross</code> or <code>xcrun metal</code> skip when</li>\n</ul>\n<p>those tools are absent.</p>\n<p>To exercise the Apple backend you need a macOS build:</p>\n<pre><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button><code>cmake --build build-apple -j8\nctest --test-dir build-apple --output-on-failure</code></pre>\n<h2 id=\"first-frame\">First frame</h2>\n<pre><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button><code>#include \"tglmt/Renderer.h\"\n#include \"tglmt/gl46.h\"\n\ntglmt::Renderer r;\nif (!r.Init(\"apple\", 960, 600, /*depth=*/true)) return 1;\n\n// All gl:: calls must come after Init / BeginFrame: they act on the current\n// Context, and BeginFrame is what makes this Renderer's Context current.\nr.BeginFrame();\n\ntglmt::gl::glViewport(0, 0, 960, 600);\ntglmt::gl::glClearColor(0.1f, 0.2f, 0.3f, 1.0f);\ntglmt::gl::glClear(0x4000 /* GL_COLOR_BUFFER_BIT */);\n\nr.EndFrame(metalLayer);   // nullptr = headless, still returns true</code></pre>\n<p>All rendering commands live in namespace <code>tglmt::gl</code> and take the same parameters as desktop OpenGL 4.6.</p>\n<h2 id=\"runtime-invariants\">Runtime invariants</h2>\n<p>Call these out before writing any code against the API:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong><code>gl::</code> calls act on the current Context.</strong> <code>Renderer::BeginFrame</code> makes the</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Renderer's Context current. Calls made before <code>Init</code>/<code>BeginFrame</code> fall through to the fallback Context and their objects land in the wrong place.</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>One Context, one thread at a time.</strong> The current Context is <code>thread_local</code>.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Applications that interleave a chunk-upload thread with the render thread must serialise externally and call <code>MakeCurrent</code> on each thread.</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong><code>Resize</code> takes effect at the next <code>BeginFrame</code>.</strong> The render target is destroyed</li>\n</ol>\n<p>immediately and rebuilt lazily; the following frame is forced to clear.</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong><code>EndFrame</code> flushes.</strong> The open render encoder and all staged buffer/texture uploads</li>\n</ol>\n<p>are flushed before the present or before a headless return.</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Colour format must match the layer.</strong> <code>Init</code> takes the pixel format; <code>presentTarget</code></li>\n</ol>\n<p>refuses a <code>CAMetalLayer</code> whose <code>pixelFormat</code> differs, which shows up as a black screen.</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong><code>BeginFrame(false)</code> must not rotate anything.</strong> That mode only re-binds the Context,</li>\n</ol>\n<p>for callers that call <code>MakeCurrent</code> in the middle of a frame. Rotating the ring or the target there corrupts the frame.</p>\n<h2 id=\"is-the-real-gpu-backend-active\">Is the real GPU backend active?</h2>\n<p>There are four independent ways to check, from cheapest to most detailed.</p>\n<pre><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button><code>r.hasRealGPU();          // C++: true only when the device is a Metal device\nr.backendName();         // C++: \"apple\", \"null\", or \"apple(fallback:null,no-MTL-device)\"</code></pre>\n<pre><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button><code>TGLMT_HasRealGPU();      // C ABI, for JNI / Objective-C launchers\nTGLMT_BackendName();     // C ABI</code></pre>\n<p>On a Null device the backend name is <code>apple(null-fallback,no-MTL-device)</code>, which is the honest signal that the \"apple\" backend was requested but no Metal device was created — either the build was configured without <code>TGLMT_APPLE_METAL</code>, or device creation failed. In that case every draw is trace-only and <code>ReadPixels</code> returns the CPU shadow, not GPU output.</p>\n<p>At runtime, stderr carries a frame summary for the first 12 swaps and then every 600th swap:</p>\n<pre><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button><code>[TGLMT] build=... frame=1 ... dAtt=... dEnc=... target=0x... WxH vp=... center=(r,g,b,a) present=1\n[TGLMT] ir frame=1 encNew=... encReuse=... pipeRe=... pipeLk=... uniRe=... stSkip=...</code></pre>\n<p><code>dAtt</code> is draws attempted, <code>dEnc</code> is draws actually encoded. If <code>dEnc</code> is 0 while <code>dAtt</code> is not, draws are being dropped — see <a href=\"compatibility.md\">Compatibility &amp; Performance</a> for the failure counters.</p>\n<h2 id=\"minimal-troubleshooting\">Minimal troubleshooting</h2>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Symptom</th><th>First check</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td><code>presentTarget</code> refuses, screen stays black</td><td><code>CAMetalLayer.pixelFormat</code> must be <code>MTLPixelFormatRGBA8Unorm</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Draws drop to zero</td><td><code>dAtt</code> vs <code>dEnc</code> in the frame summary; then <code>noProg</code>, <code>noTgt</code>, <code>noPipe</code>, <code>misc</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>ReadPixels</code> returns black or stale data</td><td><code>hasRealGPU()</code> — a Null device reads back the shadow buffer</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Tests fail to configure</td><td>CMake 3.20+ and a C++17 compiler</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>test_converter_*</code> or <code>test_spirv_chain_apple</code> skip</td><td>install <code>glslangValidator</code>, <code>spirv-cross</code>, <code>xcrun metal</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Minecraft-specific tests skip</td><td>run <code>tests/corpus/fetch-corpus.sh</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Diagnostics missing from stderr</td><td>set <code>TGLMT_DIAG=1</code>, or configure with <code>-DTGLMT_FORCE_DIAG=ON</code> for a device where the launcher cannot pass environment variables</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h2 id=\"regenerating-the-documentation-site\">Regenerating the documentation site</h2>\n<pre><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button><code>python3 tools/gen_docs_site.py</code></pre>\n<p>This reads <code>README.md</code>, <code>README.vi.md</code> and <code>docs/{en,vi}/*.md</code>, converts them to HTML, emits <code>docs/content-en.js</code>, <code>docs/content-vi.js</code> and <code>docs/nav.js</code>, and prints which files changed. After editing any canonical Markdown, run it and commit the generated files together with the source.</p>"}]}, "api": {"pages": [{"id": "api.ref", "content": "<h1 id=\"api-reference\">API Reference</h1>\n<p>TGLMT exposes four surfaces. Pick the highest level that your application can use.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Surface</th><th>Header</th><th>Use when</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td>C++ <code>Renderer</code></td><td><code>tglmt/Renderer.h</code></td><td>you own the app and can link statically or <code>dlopen</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>C++ <code>tglmt::gl</code></td><td><code>tglmt/gl46.h</code></td><td>you issue OpenGL calls from C++</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Plain C <code>gl*</code></td><td>exported symbols in <code>libtglmt.dylib</code></td><td>an existing loader resolves <code>gl*</code> by name</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Window shim</td><td><code>tglmt/GLFWShim.h</code></td><td>you need <code>CreateWindow</code> / <code>MakeContextCurrent</code> / <code>SwapBuffers</code> / <code>GetProcAddress</code></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h2 id=\"c-renderer\">C++ <code>Renderer</code></h2>\n<pre><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button><code>#include \"tglmt/Renderer.h\"\n\nclass Renderer {\npublic:\n    Renderer();\n    ~Renderer();\n\n    bool Init(const std::string&amp; backend, uint32_t w, uint32_t h,\n              bool depth = true, metal::PixelFormat fmt = metal::PixelFormat::RGBA8Unorm);\n    void Resize(uint32_t w, uint32_t h);\n\n    bool BeginFrame(bool newFrame = true);\n    bool EndFrame(void* metalLayer);   // nullptr = headless\n\n    bool ReadPixels(int x, int y, int w, int h, void* out);\n\n    Context&amp; context();\n    bool hasRealGPU() const;\n    RendererStats stats() const;\n    std::string backendName() const;\n    uint32_t width() const;\n    uint32_t height() const;\n    metal::PixelFormat colorFormat() const;\n};</code></pre>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Member</th><th>Contract</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td><code>Init</code></td><td><code>backend</code> must be <code>\"apple\"</code> or <code>\"null\"</code>; anything else returns <code>false</code>. Returns <code>false</code> on the Apple backend if the render target cannot be created. <code>fmt</code> must match the <code>CAMetalLayer.pixelFormat</code> used at present time.</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>Resize</code></td><td>records the new size, invalidates the render target and forces a full clear on the next frame. Zero dimensions are ignored.</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>BeginFrame(newFrame)</code></td><td>makes this Renderer's Context current. <code>newFrame = true</code> also rotates the upload ring. <code>newFrame = false</code> only re-binds the Context, for callers that interleave <code>MakeCurrent</code> inside a frame. Returns <code>false</code> before <code>Init</code>, or when the Apple backend has no target.</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>EndFrame(layer)</code></td><td>flushes the open encoder and all staging, then presents when <code>layer</code> is non-null. A null layer is a valid headless end-of-frame.</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>ReadPixels</code></td><td>issues <code>glReadPixels</code> on the current Context, GL-order rows (origin bottom-left), and returns <code>false</code> on a GL or parameter error.</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>hasRealGPU</code></td><td><code>true</code> only when the device is a Metal device. On <code>false</code> every draw is trace-only and <code>ReadPixels</code> reads the CPU shadow.</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>stats</code></td><td><code>RendererStats</code> mirror of the draw outcome counters.</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p><code>RendererStats</code>:</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td><code>drawsAttempted</code></td><td>draws that reached the draw path</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>drawsEncoded</code></td><td>draws that produced Metal encoding</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>noProgram</code></td><td>dropped: program missing, not linked, or has no MSL libraries</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>noTarget</code></td><td>dropped: no default render target, or wrapping it failed</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>noPipeline</code></td><td>dropped: the pipeline could not be created for this attribute layout</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>miscFail</code></td><td>dropped: everything else (VAO, buffer, encoder, commit)</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h2 id=\"opengl-c-surface\">OpenGL C++ surface</h2>\n<p>All OpenGL entry points live in namespace <code>tglmt::gl</code> and take the same parameters as desktop OpenGL 4.6:</p>\n<pre><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button><code>#include \"tglmt/gl46.h\"\n\ntglmt::gl::glGenVertexArrays(1, &amp;vao);\ntglmt::gl::glBindVertexArray(vao);\ntglmt::gl::glDrawElements(GL_TRIANGLES, 6, GL_UNSIGNED_INT, nullptr);</code></pre>\n<p><code>include/tglmt/gl46.h</code> declares <strong>698</strong> functions, generated from <code>docs/khronos/gl.xml</code> by <code>tools/gen_gl_headers.py</code>. It is paired with <code>include/tglmt/gl46_types.h</code>, which carries the GL types, enums and bitfields.</p>\n<h3 id=\"headers-in-include-tglmt\">Headers in <code>include/tglmt/</code></h3>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Header</th><th>Contents</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td><code>gl46.h</code></td><td>698 OpenGL 4.6 Core declarations in <code>tglmt::gl</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>gl46_types.h</code></td><td>GL types, constants, bitfields</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>Renderer.h</code></td><td><code>Renderer</code>, <code>RendererStats</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>GLFWShim.h</code></td><td><code>GLFWShim</code>, <code>TGLMT_Window</code>, the <code>TGLMT_*</code> C API</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>Context.h</code></td><td><code>Context</code>, <code>AppleStats</code>, object and staging tables</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>StateTracker.h</code></td><td><code>StateTracker</code>, state group types</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>ObjectRegistry.h</code></td><td><code>ObjectRegistry</code>, <code>ObjectKind</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>ErrorTracker.h</code></td><td><code>ErrorTracker</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>GLSLConverter.h</code></td><td><code>GLSLConvertResult</code>, <code>GLSLVar</code>, <code>GLSLBlock</code>, <code>ConvertGLSLtoMSL</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>GLConvert.h</code></td><td>viewport, scissor and NDC conversion helpers</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>GLAppleDraw.h</code></td><td>internal draw-path helpers</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>MetalInterface.h</code></td><td>the <code>metal::</code> backend interface (<code>IDevice</code>, <code>IRenderTarget</code>, <code>ITexture</code>, <code>IBuffer</code>, <code>IRenderPipeline</code>, …)</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h2 id=\"exported-c-api\">Exported C API</h2>\n<p><code>libtglmt.dylib</code> exports every <code>tglmt::gl</code> symbol as a plain C <code>gl*</code> function through <code>src/gl/gl_c_exports.cpp</code>, generated by <code>tools/gen_c_exports.py</code>. That is <strong>701</strong> symbols: the 698 core functions plus <code>glGetPointerv</code>, <code>glLineStipple</code> and <code>glDepthRangeArrayfvNV</code>.</p>\n<p>The library is built with default symbol visibility precisely so that an existing loader can resolve them:</p>\n<pre><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button><code>void* p = dlsym(handle, \"glDrawElements\");</code></pre>\n<p><code>GLFWShim::GetProcAddress(name)</code> performs the same lookup in-process and returns <code>NULL</code> for an unknown name.</p>\n<h2 id=\"window-shim\">Window shim</h2>\n<p><code>tglmt/GLFWShim.h</code> is the minimal surface a GLFW/LWJGL-style application needs.</p>\n<h3 id=\"c-class\">C++ class</h3>\n<pre><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button><code>class GLFWShim {\npublic:\n    static GLFWShim&amp; Instance();\n\n    TGLMT_Window* CreateWindow(uint32_t w, uint32_t h,\n                               const char* backend = \"apple\", bool depth = true);\n    void DestroyWindow(TGLMT_Window* w);\n    bool MakeCurrent(TGLMT_Window* w);\n    static void ClearCurrent();\n    bool SwapBuffers(TGLMT_Window* w, void* metalLayer);\n    void SwapInterval(int interval);\n    void* GetProcAddress(const char* name);\n    bool HasRealGPU() const;\n    uint64_t DrawsEncoded() const;\n    const char* BackendName() const;\n    void Resize(TGLMT_Window* w, uint32_t width, uint32_t height);\n};</code></pre>\n<p><code>TGLMT_Window</code> carries <code>w</code>, <code>h</code>, <code>swapInterval</code> and an opaque <code>userPtr</code>.</p>\n<h3 id=\"c-abi\">C ABI</h3>\n<p>Ten <code>extern \"C\"</code> functions, so JNI and Objective-C callers avoid name mangling:</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Function</th><th>Returns</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td><code>TGLMT_CreateWindow(w, h, backend, depth)</code></td><td><code>TGLMT_Window*</code>, or <code>NULL</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>TGLMT_DestroyWindow(w)</code></td><td>—</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>TGLMT_MakeCurrent(w)</code></td><td><code>1</code> on success, <code>0</code> on failure</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>TGLMT_ClearCurrent()</code></td><td>—</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>TGLMT_SwapBuffers(w, metalLayer)</code></td><td><code>1</code> on success, <code>0</code> on failure</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>TGLMT_SwapInterval(interval)</code></td><td>—</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>TGLMT_GetProcAddress(name)</code></td><td>function pointer, or <code>NULL</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>TGLMT_HasRealGPU()</code></td><td><code>1</code> for a Metal device, <code>0</code> otherwise</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>TGLMT_ResizeWindow(w, width, height)</code></td><td>—</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>TGLMT_BackendName()</code></td><td>diagnostic string, valid for the process lifetime</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p><code>TGLMT_BackendName()</code> returns one of <code>\"apple\"</code>, <code>\"null\"</code>, or <code>\"apple(null-fallback,no-MTL-device)\"</code>. The third value means the Apple backend was requested but no Metal device was created.</p>\n<h2 id=\"lifecycle\">Lifecycle</h2>\n<p>A complete windowed frame looks like this:</p>\n<pre><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button><code>TGLMT_Window* w = TGLMT_CreateWindow(960, 600, \"apple\", 1);\nTGLMT_MakeCurrent(w);\n\n/* every frame */\ndrawScene();                       /* any gl* calls */\nTGLMT_SwapBuffers(w, metalLayer);  /* flush + present */\n\n/* on rotation or size change */\nTGLMT_ResizeWindow(w, newW, newH); /* takes effect at the next BeginFrame */\n\nTGLMT_DestroyWindow(w);</code></pre>\n<p><code>CreateWindow</code> makes the Context current before it returns, so the first <code>gl*</code> call is already valid.</p>\n<h2 id=\"context-and-current-thread-behaviour\">Context and current-thread behaviour</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The current Context is <code>thread_local</code>. Each thread must call <code>MakeCurrent</code> itself.</li>\n<li>One Context may be used by one thread at a time. An application that runs a chunk-upload</li>\n</ul>\n<p>thread alongside the render thread must serialise the two externally and call <code>MakeCurrent</code> on each thread around its work.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>CreateWindow</code> and <code>SwapBuffers</code> take an internal lock; the rest of the GL surface does</li>\n</ul>\n<p>not.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>There is no share-list. Objects created on one Context are not visible to another.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"shader-and-program-lifecycle\">Shader and program lifecycle</h2>\n<pre><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button><code>glCreateShader(type)\n  -&gt; glShaderSource\n  -&gt; glCompileShader      vertex/fragment: GLSL -&gt; MSL, ok or explicit error\n                          other stages:    COMPILE_STATUS = false, explicit log\n  -&gt; glGetShaderiv(GL_COMPILE_STATUS / GL_INFO_LOG)\n  -&gt; glCreateProgram, glAttachShader\n  -&gt; glLinkProgram        varying checks, uniform block sizes, binding assignment\n                          on a real device: MSL -&gt; MTLLibrary per stage\n  -&gt; glGetProgramiv(GL_LINK_STATUS / GL_INFO_LOG)\n  -&gt; glUseProgram, glUniform*, glBindBufferBase\n  -&gt; glDraw*\n  -&gt; glDeleteProgram / glDeleteShader</code></pre>\n<p>Uniform blocks are reported through <code>GL_ACTIVE_UNIFORM_BLOCKS</code>, <code>GL_UNIFORM_BLOCK_DATA_SIZE</code>, <code>GL_UNIFORM_BLOCK_NAME_LENGTH</code>, <code>GLGetActiveUniformBlockName</code>, <code>GLGetActiveUniformBlockiv</code> and <code>GL_UNIFORM_BLOCK_REFERENCED_BY_*</code>. <code>GL_UNIFORM_BLOCK_DATA_SIZE</code> is the std140 size rounded to a multiple of 16.</p>\n<h2 id=\"important-object-and-state-invariants\">Important object and state invariants</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>GL calls act on the current Context.</strong> Issue them after <code>Init</code>/<code>BeginFrame</code> or after</li>\n</ol>\n<p>your own <code>MakeCurrent</code>.</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Uniform block binds must be at least <code>trueSize</code> bytes.</strong> A buffer bound with the</li>\n</ol>\n<p>struct's natural size is uploaded with zero padding to the std140 size; a buffer smaller than the natural struct size is a genuine mis-bind and is replaced by zeros so that a stray buffer cannot drive shader behaviour.</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>A texture re-specified while it is the current render target flushes first.</strong> Staged</li>\n</ol>\n<p>regions from the previous specification are discarded.</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong><code>glGetTexImage</code> / <code>glReadPixels</code> return GL-order data</strong> (row 0 is the bottom row).</li>\n<li><strong>Sampler bindings are per texture unit</strong> and are resolved at draw time from the</li>\n</ol>\n<p>program's declared sampler uniforms.</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Object ids are never reused inside a Context.</strong> The registry allocates monotonically;</li>\n</ol>\n<p>a stale id simply does not resolve.</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Deleting a bound object unbinds it</strong> across every target slot that referenced it.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"diagnostic-counters\">Diagnostic counters</h2>\n<p><code>Context::AppleStats</code> carries the per-frame instrumentation. The most useful fields when reading a log are grouped as follows:</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Group</th><th>Fields</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td>Draw outcome</td><td><code>drawsAttempted</code>, <code>drawsEncoded</code>, <code>noProgram</code>, <code>noTarget</code>, <code>noPipeline</code>, <code>miscFail</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Batching</td><td><code>encodersCreated</code>, <code>encoderReused</code>, <code>pipelineReused</code>, <code>pipelineLookups</code>, <code>pipelineLookupSkipped</code>, <code>uniformReused</code>, <code>depthReused</code>, <code>stateSkipped</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Staging</td><td><code>bufferCoalesced</code>, <code>bufferFlushes</code>, <code>texCoalesced</code>, <code>texFlushes</code>, <code>flushAvoided</code>, <code>bufRotated</code>, <code>bufWaitStall</code>, <code>texWaitStall</code>, <code>texWasRTFlush</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Ring / allocations</td><td><code>ringAllocs</code>, <code>ringWraps</code>, <code>tempAllocs</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Synchronisation</td><td><code>framesThrottled</code>, <code>cbCommittedNow</code>, <code>cbCompletedNow</code>, <code>hazardSplits</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Safety</td><td><code>rangeWarn</code>, <code>hazardWarn</code>, <code>uboSmall</code>, <code>uboPad</code>, <code>mipBase</code>, <code>mipLevelSkipped</code>, <code>mipStaged</code>, <code>clearRegionFails</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Present</td><td><code>presentPasses</code>, <code>glClears</code>, <code>blits</code>, <code>copyTex</code></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>See <a href=\"compatibility.md\">Compatibility &amp; Performance</a> for how to read them.</p>\n<h2 id=\"further-reference\">Further reference</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>docs/mapping/GL46_to_Metal.md</code> — per-function strategy table, technical reference only.</li>\n<li><code>docs/khronos/gl.xml</code> — the OpenGL registry the headers are generated from.</li>\n<li><code>shaders/*.metal</code> — hand-written Metal shaders used by native paths and tests.</li>\n</ul>"}]}, "architecture": {"pages": [{"id": "arch.overview", "content": "<h1 id=\"architecture\">Architecture</h1>\n<p>This page describes the runtime path of a single OpenGL call, from the entry point to Metal work, and the deferred-execution model that batches it.</p>\n<h2 id=\"layers\">Layers</h2>\n<pre><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button><code>  Application  (LWJGL / GLFW / Blaze3D / direct gl:: calls)\n      |\n      |  698 gl* entry points              include/tglmt/gl46.h\n      |  10 TGLMT_* window functions        include/tglmt/GLFWShim.h\n      v\n  +---------------------------------------------------------------------+\n  | Dispatch        src/gl/*.cpp                                         |\n  |   argument validation, GL error recording, shadow-state updates      |\n  |   gl_shader.cpp      glCompileShader  -&gt; GLSL-&gt;MSL                   |\n  |   gl_program.cpp     glLinkProgram    -&gt; link checks + MSL compile   |\n  |   gl_apple_draw.cpp  glDraw*          -&gt; deferred Metal encode       |\n  |   gl_texture.cpp / gl_buffer.cpp / gl_framebuffer.cpp / gl_raster.cpp|\n  +---------------------------------------------------------------------+\n      |\n      |  include/tglmt/\n      |    StateTracker.h    CPU shadow of GL state, dirty flags\n      |    ObjectRegistry.h  id -&gt; object tables (mutex protected)\n      |    ErrorTracker.h    FIFO GL error queue\n      |    Context.h         per-context everything (buffers, textures,\n      |                      programs, FBOs, staging maps, AppleStats)\n      v\n  +---------------------------------------------------------------------+\n  | GLSL -&gt; MSL     src/gl/glsl_to_msl.cpp                               |\n  |   vertex + fragment only; emits TGLMT_vs / TGLMT_fs                 |\n  +---------------------------------------------------------------------+\n      |\n      v\n  Deferred draw path     src/gl/gl_apple_draw.cpp\n      |    state shadowing and redundant-state suppression\n      |    encoder reuse across consecutive draws\n      |    pipeline-key cache, uniform cache\n      |    buffer/texture staging with range coalescing\n      |    ring-buffer uploads, conditional flushes\n      v\n  Metal abstraction      include/tglmt/MetalInterface.h\n      |\n      +--&gt; src/metal/AppleMetalBridge.mm   Apple backend, real GPU\n      +--&gt; src/metal/NullMetalBackend.cpp  Null backend, trace + shadow\n      v\n  presentTarget(CAMetalLayer)     or     readback from the shadow buffer</code></pre>\n<p>Two backends implement the same <code>metal::IDevice</code> interface. The backend is chosen when the Context is constructed from the string <code>\"apple\"</code> or <code>\"null\"</code>; a request for <code>\"apple\"</code> that cannot create a Metal device falls back to the Null device and reports itself as <code>apple(null-fallback,no-MTL-device)</code>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"context-and-state\">Context and state</h2>\n<p><code>Context</code> owns every object table (buffers, textures, samplers, programs, FBOs, VAOs, transform-feedback objects), both staging maps, the ring allocator, the pipeline caches and <code>AppleStats</code>.</p>\n<p><code>StateTracker</code> holds the CPU shadow of GL state. Its groups are:</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Group</th><th>Contents</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td>Capabilities</td><td><code>glEnable</code> / <code>glEnablei</code> per target</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Blend and colour mask</td><td>per-attachment blend state and 4-bit colour masks</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Depth and stencil</td><td>depth func/enable/write, front and back stencil</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Raster</td><td>viewports, cull mode, front face, polygon mode, scissor, polygon offset, line width, clip control</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Bindings</td><td>buffer binding points, per-unit texture slots and sampler bindings, active texture unit, bound VAO, program, XFB, read/draw FBO, patch vertices</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Pixel store</td><td>pack/unpack row length, skip, alignment</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Get-shadow</td><td><code>(pname, index)</code> values returned by <code>glGet*</code></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Every setter compares before assigning. <code>SetEnabled</code>, <code>SetBlendColor</code>, <code>SetViewport</code>, <code>SetScissor</code>, <code>SetLineWidth</code>, <code>SetDepthRangef</code>, <code>SetPatchVertices</code> and <code>BindXFB</code> all return early when the value is unchanged, which also means <code>stateSeq_</code> does not advance. <code>stateSeq_</code> is therefore a direct measurement of \"N identical GL calls produced zero state changes\".</p>\n<p>All <code>glGet*</code> calls read the shadow; none of them round-trips to the GPU (<code>src/gl/gl_get.cpp</code>).</p>\n<h2 id=\"object-registry\">Object registry</h2>\n<p><code>ObjectRegistry</code> is a mutex-protected <code>id -&gt; object</code> table with a monotonically increasing next id, used for buffers, textures, samplers, programs, shaders, framebuffers, VAOs and transform-feedback objects. Deletion removes the table entry; the per-context maps (<code>c.buffers</code>, <code>c.textures</code>, …) hold the actual payload.</p>\n<h2 id=\"shader-and-program-system\">Shader and program system</h2>\n<p><code>glCompileShader</code> routes vertex and fragment shaders to <code>ConvertGLSLtoMSL</code>. Any other stage — tessellation control, tessellation evaluation, geometry, compute — is rejected at compile time with <code>COMPILE_STATUS = false</code> and an explicit log (<code>src/gl/gl_shader.cpp</code>). Nothing is silently approximated at this level.</p>\n<p><code>glLinkProgram</code> then:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>checks varying name/location/type agreement between vertex outputs and fragment inputs;</li>\n<li>checks that every fragment input is written by the vertex stage;</li>\n<li>computes <code>trueSize</code> (largest member end offset) and <code>minSize</code> (that value rounded up to</li>\n</ol>\n<p>16) for each uniform block;</p>\n<ol>\n<li>assigns uniform block bindings from <code>layout(binding=N)</code> or from a previous</li>\n</ol>\n<p><code>glUniformBlockBinding</code>;</p>\n<ol>\n<li>on a real device, compiles the generated MSL to <code>MTLLibrary</code> objects and stores them on</li>\n</ol>\n<p>the program. On a Null device this step is skipped entirely.</p>\n<p>A program with tessellation or geometry stages, or a vertex-only program, links successfully because the OpenGL specification requires it, but the draw path then declines to encode and counts the attempt as trace-only.</p>\n<p>Pipeline state objects are created lazily on first use and pre-warmed by <code>Context::PrewarmPipelineForProgram</code> before the first frame.</p>\n<h2 id=\"draw-call-lifecycle\">Draw-call lifecycle</h2>\n<p><code>glDrawArrays</code> / <code>glDrawElements</code> and their variants converge on <code>AppleDrawGL</code> (<code>src/gl/gl_apple_draw.cpp</code>). In order:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Reject early</strong> — no current target, <code>baseInstance != 0</code>, a program that is not linked,</li>\n</ol>\n<p>a program with tessellation/geometry stages, <code>GL_PATCHES</code>, non-zero <code>baseVertex</code> on a non-indexed draw. Each rejection increments a dedicated counter rather than silently dropping the work.</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Resolve resources</strong> — vertex array, element array, bound program, colour and depth</li>\n</ol>\n<p>attachments of the currently bound draw FBO.</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Hazard pre-scan</strong> — if the program samples the very texture it renders into, the open</li>\n</ol>\n<p>encoder is ended first and <code>hazardSplits</code> increments. This is a TBDR requirement: Metal has no automatic read-write hazard tracking for the same resource in one render pass.</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Choose or create the render encoder</strong> — reuse when the open encoder exists and the</li>\n</ol>\n<p>draw FBO, colour attachment, depth presence and pending clear all match; otherwise flush the old encoder and create a new one.</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Clear</strong> — an immediate clear is issued when possible; if not, the clear is recorded as</li>\n</ol>\n<p><code>applePendingClear</code> and consumed by the next draw as <code>loadAction = Clear</code>.</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Resolve the pipeline</strong> — a <code>Context::PipelineKey</code> (vertex/fragment libraries, format,</li>\n</ol>\n<p>vertex stride, depth, blend, colour write mask, and the full vertex attribute layout) is compared against a cache. A hit skips the bridge call entirely; a miss calls <code>makeCustomPipeline</code>.</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Upload uniforms</strong> — the per-stage uniform byte buffer is compared against</li>\n</ol>\n<p><code>uniformCache</code> and only a changed stage is re-uploaded. Uniform data comes from the ring allocator.</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Encode state</strong> — viewport, scissor, cull, fill mode, blend, depth, colour mask are</li>\n</ol>\n<p>written to the encoder only when the pending-encoder shadow says the value changed.</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Encode the draw</strong> — FAN and LOOP primitives are expanded into triangles on the CPU</li>\n</ol>\n<p>first, because Metal has neither.</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Record usage</strong> — the buffers and textures the draw consumed are appended to the</li>\n</ol>\n<p>pending-usage lists that gate later conditional flushes.</p>\n<h2 id=\"deferred-execution\">Deferred execution</h2>\n<p>TGLMT does not issue one Metal command per OpenGL call. Three independent mechanisms defer work.</p>\n<h3 id=\"encoder-lifetime\">Encoder lifetime</h3>\n<p>A single <code>MTLRenderCommandEncoder</code> stays open across consecutive draws that belong to the same render pass. It is ended only when something invalidates the pass:</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Trigger</th><th>Site</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td>Draw FBO, colour attachment or depth presence changes</td><td><code>gl_apple_draw.cpp</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Feedback hazard detected by the pre-scan</td><td><code>gl_apple_draw.cpp</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Immediate clear</td><td><code>gl_apple_draw.cpp</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Framebuffer blit, <code>glReadPixels</code>, <code>glGetTexImage</code>, <code>glCopyTexSubImage2D</code></td><td><code>gl_framebuffer.cpp</code>, <code>gl_readpixels_dsa.cpp</code>, <code>gl_get_extra.cpp</code>, <code>gl_texture.cpp</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>A texture that is the current render target is re-specified</td><td><code>gl_texture.cpp</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Staging of a resource already used in the open pass</td><td><code>gl_buffer.cpp</code>, <code>gl_texture.cpp</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>glFlush</code> / <code>glFinish</code></td><td><code>gl_sync_query.cpp</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Frame boundary — <code>SwapBuffers</code>, <code>EndFrame</code>, <code>Resize</code></td><td><code>glfw_shim.cpp</code>, <code>Renderer.cpp</code></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p><code>encodersCreated</code> versus <code>encoderReused</code> in the frame summary is the direct measurement of batching: a healthy frame has <code>encReuse</code> far larger than <code>encNew</code>.</p>\n<h3 id=\"resource-staging\">Resource staging</h3>\n<p><code>glBufferSubData</code> and <code>glTexSubImage2D</code> do not touch the GPU immediately. They append to <code>pendingBufRanges</code> / <code>pendingTexRegions</code>. Adjacent ranges are merged (buffer gap up to 64 bytes; texture regions into a bounding box) before one <code>memcpy</code> and one <code>didModifyRange</code> / <code>replaceRegion</code>.</p>\n<p>Staging only breaks batching when the resource has *already* been used by the open pass. <code>MustFlushForBufferStage</code> and <code>MustFlushForTextureStage</code> check the pending-usage lists, and a declined flush increments <code>flushAvoided</code>. This is what lets thousands of uploads coexist with encoder batching.</p>\n<p>In-flight protection uses a three-slot buffer pool; a slot the GPU is still reading is not written. If no slot is free, TGLMT commits and waits (<code>bufWaitStall</code>) instead of corrupting data. Textures equivalent: <code>texWasRTFlush</code> when the only copy lives on the GPU.</p>\n<h3 id=\"frame-boundary\">Frame boundary</h3>\n<p><code>SwapBuffers</code> and <code>EndFrame</code> flush the encoder and all staging, then call <code>ThrottleGpu()</code>, which blocks only when the number of command buffers in flight exceeds <code>kMaxFramesInFlight</code> (2). There is no <code>commitAndWait</code> per frame: Metal executes command buffers on one queue in submission order, so frame N+1 cannot observe frame N's writes early.</p>\n<h2 id=\"pipeline-caching\">Pipeline caching</h2>\n<p>Three layers avoid redundant work:</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Layer</th><th>Key</th><th>Counter</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td>IR pipeline key</td><td>libraries, format, stride, depth, blend, colour mask, attribute layout</td><td><code>pipelineLookupSkipped</code> on hit, <code>pipelineLookups</code> on miss</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Bridge PSO cache</td><td>descriptor identity inside <code>AppleMetalBridge.mm</code></td><td><code>pipelineLookups</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Encoder-local reuse</td><td>identical <code>nativeHandle()</code> within one pass</td><td><code>pipelineReused</code></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Depth-stencil states are cached the same way and counted as <code>depthReused</code>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"ring-buffer-uploads\">Ring-buffer uploads</h2>\n<p><code>Context</code> owns three 4 MB shared <code>MTLBuffer</code> objects rotated per frame (<code>kRingFrames = 3</code>, <code>kRingSize = 4 MB</code>, 256-byte alignment). Uniform data, temporary index buffers and FAN/LOOP expansions are bump-allocated from the current slot, which keeps per-frame <code>MTLBuffer</code> allocations at zero (<code>ringAllocs</code>); the fallback count is <code>tempAllocs</code>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"synchronization-boundaries\">Synchronization boundaries</h2>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Mechanism</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td><code>cbCommitted</code> / <code>cbCompleted</code></td><td>atomics bumped per command-buffer commit and per completion handler</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>GpuBusy()</code></td><td><code>cbCommitted &gt; cbCompleted</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>ThrottleGpu()</code></td><td>blocks only when in-flight work exceeds <code>kMaxFramesInFlight</code>; counted as <code>framesThrottled</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>Context::CommitAndWait()</code></td><td>the only permitted path to a blocking commit-and-wait; bumps <code>waitGen</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>FlushPendingEncoder()</code></td><td>ends the open encoder and commits without waiting</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>glFinish()</code></td><td>encoder + all staging + <code>CommitAndWait()</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>glFlush()</code></td><td>encoder + all staging, no wait</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p><code>CommitAndWait</code> must be used for every blocking wait so that <code>waitGen</code> stays accurate; bypassing it makes the buffer pool orphan unnecessarily.</p>\n<h2 id=\"coordinate-conversion\">Coordinate conversion</h2>\n<p><code>include/tglmt/GLConvert.h</code> contains the pure-CPU conversions:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Viewport</strong> — OpenGL's origin is the lower left and Metal's is the upper left, so a</li>\n</ul>\n<p><code>GL_LOWER_LEFT</code> viewport becomes <code>y = targetHeight - (y + h)</code>. Under <code>GL_UPPER_LEFT</code> (<code>glClipControl</code>) the values pass through unchanged.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Depth range</strong> — <code>GL_NEGATIVE_ONE_TO_ONE</code> maps <code>z</code> from <code>[-1,1]</code> to <code>[0,1]</code>;</li>\n</ul>\n<p><code>GL_ZERO_TO_ONE</code> passes through.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Scissor</strong> — identity, with only negative-coordinate clamping.</li>\n<li><strong>Shader Z</strong> — the converter appends a depth conversion to the vertex stage unless the</li>\n</ul>\n<p>program uses <code>GL_ZERO_TO_ONE</code>.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Present</strong> — memory is GL-order (row 0 is the bottom). The present pass draws a</li>\n</ul>\n<p>full-screen triangle that samples the target with a flipped V, so one draw produces the vertical flip. If that pipeline cannot be created, present falls back to a per-row blit that is always correct but much slower.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Readback</strong> — <code>glReadPixels</code> flushes the GPU and returns GL-order rows.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"framebuffer-and-texture-handling\">Framebuffer and texture handling</h2>\n<p>FBOs are resolved to a concrete colour texture (plus optional depth texture) at draw time. Attachment with a mip level greater than 0 records the level on the attachment; the render target is sized <code>base &gt;&gt; level</code>. Drawing or clearing into mip level greater than 0 of a single-level texture is skipped and counted as <code>mipLevelSkipped</code>.</p>\n<p>Texture uploads honour <code>glPixelStorei</code> pack/unpack row length, skip and alignment. Pixel formats are mapped from GL internal format to <code>metal::PixelFormat</code> at texture creation; a re-specification of a texture that is currently the render target flushes the pending encoder first and discards its staged regions.</p>\n<p><code>glBlitFramebuffer</code>, <code>glCopyTexSubImage2D</code> and <code>glGetTexImage</code> are implemented as GPU-side copies where formats match and fall back to a CPU copy otherwise.</p>\n<h2 id=\"error-handling\">Error handling</h2>\n<p><code>ErrorTracker</code> is a mutex-protected FIFO of GL error codes. <code>glGetError</code> pops from the front, matching the specification. The first ten recorded errors are logged with a backtrace so the offending caller can be located.</p>\n<p><code>glGetString</code> reports vendor <code>TGLMT</code>, renderer <code>Apple GPU (Metal)</code>, version <code>4.6 (TGLMT Metal port, build &lt;N&gt;.&lt;hash&gt;)</code> — the build-number suffix is generated from git at configure time (<code>cmake/tglmt_buildinfo.h.in</code>) and shows up on F3 via <code>GpuDevice.getVersion</code> — and shading-language version <code>4.60 (TGLMT MSL)</code>. The extension list is deliberately fixed at six entries; the returned list is what LWJGL builds its capability set from.</p>\n<p>Diagnostic logging is gated by <code>Context::DiagOn()</code>: the environment variable <code>TGLMT_DIAG=1</code> for a normal build, or configure with <code>-DTGLMT_FORCE_DIAG=ON</code> when the process cannot be given environment variables. Diagnostics skipped while the gate is closed are counted (<code>diagSkipped</code>), not silently discarded.</p>\n<h2 id=\"where-each-subsystem-lives\">Where each subsystem lives</h2>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Subsystem</th><th>Files</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td>Renderer façade</td><td><code>src/core/Renderer.cpp</code>, <code>include/tglmt/Renderer.h</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Context, staging, caches, counters</td><td><code>src/core/Context.cpp</code>, <code>include/tglmt/Context.h</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Shadow state</td><td><code>src/core/StateTracker.cpp</code>, <code>include/tglmt/StateTracker.h</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Object tables, error queue</td><td><code>src/core/ObjectRegistry.cpp</code>, <code>src/core/ErrorTracker.cpp</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>GL dispatch</td><td><code>src/gl/gl_*.cpp</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>GLSL to MSL</td><td><code>src/gl/glsl_to_msl.cpp</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Deferred draw path</td><td><code>src/gl/gl_apple_draw.cpp</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>C exports, window shim</td><td><code>src/gl/gl_c_exports.cpp</code>, <code>src/gl/glfw_shim.cpp</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Metal abstraction</td><td><code>include/tglmt/MetalInterface.h</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Apple backend</td><td><code>src/metal/AppleMetalBridge.mm</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Null backend</td><td><code>src/metal/NullMetalBackend.cpp</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Coordinate conversion</td><td><code>include/tglmt/GLConvert.h</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Hand-written Metal shaders</td><td><code>shaders/*.metal</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Header generators</td><td><code>tools/gen_gl_headers.py</code>, <code>tools/gen_c_exports.py</code>, <code>tools/gen_stubs.py</code></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>"}]}, "launcher": {"pages": [{"id": "launcher.integration", "content": "<h1 id=\"embedding-in-an-ios-launcher\">Embedding in an iOS launcher</h1>\n<p>Reference integration: <code>Natives/ctxbridges/tglmt_bridge.m</code> in the Angel-Aura-Amethyst-iOS launcher (renderer key <code>libtglmt.dylib</code>).</p>\n<h2 id=\"1-ship-the-dylib\">1. Ship the dylib</h2>\n<p>Build the arm64 dylib (see <code>getting-started.md</code>) and embed as <code>Frameworks/libtglmt.dylib</code>. It links only system frameworks (Metal, Foundation, QuartzCore).</p>\n<h2 id=\"2-renderer-selection\">2. Renderer selection</h2>\n<p>Expose <code>libtglmt.dylib</code> in the renderer picker next to the existing backends. On select, before JVM start:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>dlopen(Frameworks/libtglmt.dylib, RTLD_GLOBAL)</code> so both the bridge and</li>\n</ul>\n<p>LWJGL resolve the same image.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Set <code>org.lwjgl.opengl.libname</code> to the absolute Frameworks path. Absolute</li>\n</ul>\n<p>matters: a bare name lets a stale same-named file in the natives dir shadow the signed copy and <code>GL.create()</code> fails with <code>error=null</code>.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Install a bridge table `{init, init_context, make_current, swap_buffers,</li>\n</ul>\n<p>swap_interval, terminate}<code> backed by the </code>TGLMT_*` C API. No EGL is involved on this path.</p>\n<h2 id=\"3-surface-rules\">3. Surface rules</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Layer class must be <code>CAMetalLayer</code> (same as other Metal renderers).</li>\n<li>Set <code>layer.pixelFormat = RGBA8Unorm</code> — TGLMT refuses to present on</li>\n</ul>\n<p>mismatch (returns false, black screen if ignored). ANGLE needs BGRA8, so branch per renderer.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>layer.framebufferOnly = NO</code> (blit present + readback path).</li>\n<li>Ensure non-zero <code>drawableSize</code> before creating the TGLMT window.</li>\n<li>Forward rotation/resize to <code>TGLMT_ResizeWindow</code>; otherwise presents</li>\n</ul>\n<p>letterbox into the old-size target.</p>\n<h2 id=\"4-threading-phase-1\">4. Threading (phase 1)</h2>\n<p>One shared <code>Context</code>, serialized: the render thread and the chunk-uploader thread each call <code>TGLMT_MakeCurrent</code> around their GL work and never draw concurrently. True share-lists (parallel upload + render) are a later stage; persistent-mapping flags are currently accepted but not fenced, so throttle uploads on the launcher side.</p>\n<h2 id=\"5-first-launch-checklist\">5. First-launch checklist</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><code>[TGLMT] dlopen OK</code> in the log; <code>HasRealGPU</code> true on device.</li>\n<li><code>drawsEncoded == drawsAttempted</code> after the first frames.</li>\n<li>Pixels: clear color visible, then textured quad, then world.</li>\n<li>On black screen, check in order: pixel-format match, non-zero layer</li>\n</ol>\n<p>size, program link log (<code>glGetProgramInfoLog</code>), then stats counters.</p>"}]}, "limits": {"pages": [{"id": "limits.ref", "content": "<h1 id=\"limits-honest\">Limits (honest)</h1>\n<p>Decl coverage is 100% (698 core + 3 compat/extension extras, verified via symbol table). Behavior coverage is not: entries below are no-ops, trace-only, or CPU approximations. Anything outside the converter subset fails compile with a log instead of generating guessed code.</p>\n<h2 id=\"renders-correctly\">Renders correctly</h2>\n<p>VAO/VBO/EBO, <code>DrawArrays/Elements</code> (+<code>BaseVertex</code>, instanced, indirect, multi), <code>FAN</code>/<code>LOOP</code> expansion, primitive restart split, UBYTE indices, depth test, per-target blend (attachment 0 on the GL path), cull, wireframe fill, scissor, samplers + anisotropy, sRGB/R8/RG8 formats, MSAA resolve on the direct path, <code>BlitFramebuffer</code> (same-size NEAREST on GPU, scaled on CPU), mipmap generation, <code>ReadPixels</code>/<code>GetTexImage</code> roundtrip.</p>\n<h2 id=\"stubbed-or-approximated\">Stubbed or approximated</h2>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Area</th><th>Behavior</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td>Tessellation / geometry stages</td><td>Compile fails honestly; Metal has no such stages (see HONESTLY_ABSENT.md)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Compute stage</td><td>✅ Works (P6f): kernel, SSBO, image, dispatch — ARB_compute_shader</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Transform feedback</td><td>State machine + draw count only, no varying capture</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>glLogicOp</code></td><td>Shadow only (compute-ROP shader exists but is not wired to draws)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Stencil test</td><td>GPU: encoded in depth-stencil state; a single Metal reference value is shared by front/back faces</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>glColorMask</code></td><td>No-op (no write-mask bake)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Per-attachment blend beyond 0, <code>ClearBuffer</code> on MRT &gt; 0</td><td>Single-target only</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Compressed / 3D / multisample texture storage</td><td>Compressed and MSAA 3D/array rejected; 2D MSAA, 3D textures and mip chains implemented</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>ReadPixels</code></td><td>RGBA/BGRA + <code>UNSIGNED_BYTE</code> only</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Dual-source blend factors</td><td>Fall back to ONE/ADD</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>baseInstance != 0</code></td><td>GPU via <code>drawIndexedBaseInstance</code> / <code>drawPrimitivesBaseInstance</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>UNSIGNED_INT_10F_11F_11F_REV</code> packed vertex</td><td>Normalized approximation, logged</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h2 id=\"device-notes-a11-baseline\">Device notes (A11 baseline)</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Mesh shaders need Apple7+ (A17/M3); vanilla does not use them.</li>\n<li>iOS forbids <code>Depth24Unorm_Stencil8</code>; TGLMT maps it to</li>\n</ul>\n<p><code>Depth32Float_Stencil8</code> automatically.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>generateMipmaps</code> needs a mipmapped texture; single-level textures keep</li>\n</ul>\n<p>the base level (renders, may shimmer).</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Deferred command queue is ON: N draws on the same target share 1</li>\n</ul>\n<p><code>MTLRenderCommandEncoder</code> (see <code>docs/en/perf.md</code> + <code>test_perf_deferred_apple</code>). Budget still matters on A11 — FBO thrash or feedback loops split passes. Set <code>TGLMT_DIAG=1</code> only for debugging (release stays quiet for 60fps).</p>\n<h2 id=\"roadmap-pointer\">Roadmap pointer</h2>\n<p>Sodium/Iris stage: tessellation factors from TCS, geometry via mesh prepass (Apple7+) or CPU fallback, real compute dispatch, parallel share-lists with fencing, UBO <code>std140</code> layout audit. See <code>ROADMAP.md</code> for the full plan and <code>COVERAGE.md</code> for reproduction commands.</p>"}]}, "perf": {"pages": [{"id": "perf.deferred", "content": "<h1 id=\"performance-deferred-full-honest-numbers\">Performance (deferred full — honest numbers)</h1>\n<p>Target: Minecraft Java vanilla on iPhone A11+ (TBDR) and MacIntel (IMR/discrete), both real Metal. Null backend stays green on CI (logic only).</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-was-slow-1-gl-10-20-metal-measured-before-fix\">What was slow (1 GL → ~10-20 Metal, measured before fix)</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>EmitDraw</code> created a trace <code>IEncoder</code> AND encoded GPU work per draw</li>\n</ul>\n<p>(double-encoder on Apple).</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Every draw did 2× <code>newBufferWithBytes</code> (uniforms) + N× UBO uploads +</li>\n</ul>\n<p>index-rewrite alloc + <code>makeCustomPipeline</code> string-build + mutex, even when nothing changed.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>StageBufferRange</code>/<code>StageTexRegion</code> flushed the open encoder on EVERY</li>\n</ul>\n<p><code>SubData</code>, even for buffers not used in the pass → <code>encodersCreated ≈ draws</code>.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Hot-path diagnostics: <code>fprintf</code> per unique combo, 256×256 GUI-texture</li>\n</ul>\n<p><code>wrapAsTarget+readback</code> INSIDE draw (sync stall), 32k-index scan per draw, full draw-state dump with GPU readback.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>blitCopy</code>/<code>generateMipmaps</code>/<code>CopyFB</code> used <code>commit+waitUntilCompleted</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p>inside frame (CPU idle, GPU starved — WWDC19 anti-pattern).</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-changed-this-patch\">What changed (this patch)</h2>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Fix</th><th>File</th><th>Counter</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td>Skip trace encoder on Apple (<code>traceSkipped</code>)</td><td><code>src/gl/gl_draw.cpp</code></td><td><code>traceSkipped</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Conditional-flush staging (<code>flushAvoided</code>)</td><td><code>gl_buffer/texture.cpp</code>, <code>Context</code> used-sets</td><td><code>flushAvoided</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Triple-buffer ring 3×4MB, 0 alloc steady-state</td><td><code>Context::RingAlloc</code>, <code>gl_apple_draw</code> uniforms/UBO/index</td><td><code>ringAllocs</code>, <code>tempAllocs==0</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Pipeline-key cache skips bridge lookup</td><td><code>Context::pendingPipeKey</code></td><td><code>pipelineLookupSkipped</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Uniform bytes cache + dirty-check state</td><td><code>uniformCache</code>, <code>pending*Valid</code></td><td><code>uniformReused</code>, <code>stateSkipped</code>, <code>depthReused</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Feedback-hazard split (TBDR correct)</td><td>pre-scan + <code>hazardSplits</code></td><td><code>hazardSplits</code>, <code>hazardWarn</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>MultiDraw batch counting</td><td><code>glMultiDraw*</code></td><td><code>multidrawBatched</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Diag gate <code>TGLMT_DIAG=1</code> (release quiet)</td><td>all <code>fprintf</code>/<code>readback</code> hot paths</td><td><code>diagSkipped</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Validator skip-after-warn (4k scan cap)</td><td>index/vertex range checks</td><td><code>rangeWarn</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Depth-state prewarm (16 states)</td><td><code>PrewarmPipelineForProgram</code></td><td><code>psoPrewarmed</code></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h2 id=\"how-to-reproduce\">How to reproduce</h2>\n<pre><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button><code># Logic + perf proof, real Metal on MacIntel\ncmake -S . -B build-apple -DTGLMT_APPLE_METAL=ON &amp;&amp; cmake --build build-apple -j8\n./build-apple/test_perf_deferred_apple   # want: 100 draws -&gt; 1 encoder, ring&gt;0, tempFallback=0\n./build-apple/test_ir_batch_apple        # 3 draws -&gt; 1 encoder\n./build-apple/test_ir_full_apple         # pipeline 1+1, buffer 10-&gt;1, tex 4-&gt;1\nctest --test-dir build-apple             # 42/42 green\n\n# Quiet release (Minecraft): no stderr spam, no readback stall\nunset TGLMT_DIAG\n# Debug on device: full dumps + GUI texture soi\nTGLMT_DIAG=1 ./build-ios-pkg/run.sh 2&gt; latestlog.txt</code></pre>\n<p>Expected <code>test_perf_deferred_apple</code> output (MacIntel, May 2026):</p>\n<pre><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button><code>batch100: enc=1 (want 1) reuse=99 traceSkip=100 ring=2 tempFallback=0 us=~2000-3000\ncond-flush: enc=1 flushAvoided&gt;=5\nused-flush: enc=2 (split on used-buffer stage)\nmultidraw: enc=1 batched=5\nmid=(255,0,0)</code></pre>\n<p><code>ring=2</code> = first draw uploads VS+FS once, 99 draws reuse (steady-state 0 alloc). <code>us</code> varies by machine; assert is on counters, not wall-clock.</p>\n<h2 id=\"budgets-a11-baseline-vanilla-64-64-fullscreen-extrapolates-linearly\">Budgets (A11 baseline, vanilla 64×64 → fullscreen extrapolates linearly)</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Encoders per frame: <code>encodersCreated &lt;&lt; drawsEncoded</code> (target &lt; draws/50).</li>\n<li>Temp allocs per frame steady-state: <code>tempAllocs == 0</code> (ring covers).</li>\n<li>Sync waits per frame: 0 except <code>ReadPixels</code>/<code>present</code> boundaries.</li>\n<li>First-frame hitch: MSL compile at <code>glLinkProgram</code> (loading screen), PSO</li>\n</ul>\n<p>descriptor build at first draw (ms). Call <code>PrewarmPipelineForProgram</code> per program during loading to warm depth cache.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>If <code>encodersCreated ≈ drawsEncoded</code>, check: FBO thrash per draw, hazard</li>\n</ul>\n<p>split storm (<code>hazardSplits</code> high = feedback loop in shaders), or staging of used buffers per draw (chunk uploader writing VBO being drawn — needs double-buffering in launcher).</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-is-still-not-deferred-honest\">What is still NOT deferred (honest)</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>glBufferData</code>/<code>glTexImage2D</code> allocate immediately (<code>newBuffer</code>/<code>newTexture</code>).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Only <code>SubData</code>/<code>TexSubImage</code> are staged. Cold-path allocs stay (correct).</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>glCopyTexSubImage</code>/<code>glBlitFramebuffer</code> scaled path uses CPU fallback +</li>\n</ul>\n<p><code>commitAndWait</code> (rare: blur/post chain). Same-size NEAREST stays GPU-only.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>PSO compile is synchronous at first draw per unique key (ms). Async compile</li>\n</ul>\n<p>with fallback PSO is roadmap (Metal4 suspend/resume, ICB for indirect).</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Fan/loop CPU expansion allocates <code>std::vector</code> per draw (rare: vanilla uses</li>\n</ul>\n<p>triangles; menu logo only).</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>ReadPixels</code>/<code>GetTexImage</code> flush + wait (correct per spec §18.2).</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"counters-context-applestats-also-via-renderer-stats-subset\">Counters (<code>Context::AppleStats</code>, also via <code>Renderer::stats</code> subset)</h2>\n<p><code>drawsAttempted/drawsEncoded/noProgram/noTarget/noPipeline/miscFail</code>, <code>encodersCreated/encoderReused/pipelineReused/stateSkipped/uniformReused/ depthReused/pipelineLookups/pipelineLookupSkipped/bufferCoalesced/ bufferFlushes/texCoalesced/texFlushes/traceSkipped/diagSkipped/ringAllocs/ ringWraps/tempAllocs/flushAvoided/hazardSplits/multidrawBatched/psoPrewarmed</code>.</p>"}]}};
